(2618433, 359270, 30861, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon! It''s a striking scene. Re: your sharpness comments, the Circle of Confusion begins to set in at about f/11-f/16 on that lens, depending on how wide you are zoomed, and CoF is particularly destructive of night scenes. You have enough DOF with the 10-22mm to essentially have 3 feet to infinity in focus at f/5.6 or f/8, so it shouldn''t have been an issue. You could have run this at ISO 100 and f/8 if you''d chosen to. Also, I almost never use autofocus at night (unclear if you did), preferring to use a small penlight to set the focus manually by distance on the lens.</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon! It''s a striking scene. Re: your sharpness comments, the Circle of Confusion begins to set in at about f/11-f/16 on that lens, depending on how wide you are zoomed, and CoF is particularly destructive of night scenes. You have enough DOF with the 10-22mm to essentially have 3 feet to infinity in focus at f/5.6 or f/8, so it shouldn''t have been an issue. You could have run this at ISO 100 and f/8 if you''d chosen to. Also, I almost never use autofocus at night (unclear if you did), preferring to use a small penlight to set the focus manually by distance on the lens.', '2006-07-13 10:54:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2618436, 358776, 30861, '<td valign="top">Congrats on top 5, Julie!</td>', 'Congrats on top 5, Julie!', '2006-07-13 10:55:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2618440, 358705, 30861, '<td valign="top">Congrats on top 5! I''d actually expected this to ribbon... It was close :-)</td>', 'Congrats on top 5! I''d actually expected this to ribbon... It was close :-)', '2006-07-13 10:55:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2618443, 359005, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''m delighted to see this totally out-of-the-box take on fireworks do so well! NO color? REVERSED? You got to be kidding! jejeje</td>', 'I''m delighted to see this totally out-of-the-box take on fireworks do so well! NO color? REVERSED? You got to be kidding! jejeje', '2006-07-13 10:57:06.000000', NULL, 0),
