(2622535, 358998, 39880, '<td valign="top">Hey Cutter, great shot.  I wish I was there, but I was stuck at work.  Thanks for showing me what I missed.  Looks like a good crowd.</td>', 'Hey Cutter, great shot.  I wish I was there, but I was stuck at work.  Thanks for showing me what I missed.  Looks like a good crowd.', '2006-07-14 15:01:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2622841, 359316, 7364, '<td valign="top">Hi, There, I''ve got this same camera and it really sucks with noise with anything over 1 second.  The in-camera noise reduction filter does work pretty good though.  I''ve played around with it a little bit.  I can''t remember where it is off the top of my head but it''s not too hard to find.  For images that have alot of noise, it takes 1 to 2 seconds longer to store the image, but it''s worth it in a pinch.  It works good in low light up to about 8 seconds, them it still leaves some noise behind... but it''s still better than without it.</td>', 'Hi, There, I''ve got this same camera and it really sucks with noise with anything over 1 second.  The in-camera noise reduction filter does work pretty good though.  I''ve played around with it a little bit.  I can''t remember where it is off the top of my head but it''s not too hard to find.  For images that have alot of noise, it takes 1 to 2 seconds longer to store the image, but it''s worth it in a pinch.  It works good in low light up to about 8 seconds, them it still leaves some noise behind... but it''s still better than without it.', '2006-07-14 16:59:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2623455, 357974, 41337, '<td valign="top">Hehehe, this is very Rikki-like in so many ways.</td>', 'Hehehe, this is very Rikki-like in so many ways.', '2006-07-14 21:39:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2624063, 359270, 18461, '<td valign="top">Great shot.  Try doing a mirror lock up on long exposures.  The camera shakes when you hit the shutter which will cause stationary things to blur.  Also, if you have a cable release or remote for it, use that too to cut down on the vibrations.</td>', 'Great shot.  Try doing a mirror lock up on long exposures.  The camera shakes when you hit the shutter which will cause stationary things to blur.  Also, if you have a cable release or remote for it, use that too to cut down on the vibrations.', '2006-07-15 01:49:22.000000', NULL, 0),
