(2625753, 359005, 39007, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mo5988:</b></div><hr/><i> what are "multiple accounts?" anyone?<br/> <br/>what a disappointment! i wish this had ribboned </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Multiple accounts = one person with more than one username, allows things like voting on your own images which is obviously not fair...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-15 23:39:46.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by mo5988: what are "multiple accounts?" anyone? what a disappointment! i wish this had ribboned   Multiple accounts = one person with more than one username, allows things like voting on your own images which is obviously not fair...', '2006-07-15 23:36:38.000000', '2006-07-16 00:39:46.000000', 0),
(2626103, 359293, 37858, '<td valign="top">I voted 6 for this image because I liked the clarity and colors.  The complementary green and red was a bonus as far as I am concerned.  I would have preferred to have the people in the image too, as I think fireworks are even more dramatic when there is a frame of reference.  I would not have added the frame, but I didn''t mark down because of it.</td>', 'I voted 6 for this image because I liked the clarity and colors.  The complementary green and red was a bonus as far as I am concerned.  I would have preferred to have the people in the image too, as I think fireworks are even more dramatic when there is a frame of reference.  I would not have added the frame, but I didn''t mark down because of it.', '2006-07-16 02:31:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626724, 358998, 55642, '<td valign="top">For those curious, I suspect it was the upper portion of the scoreboard, which you can see here in this daytime photo taken from a fairly similar angle: <a href="//www.photofile.com/Photos/Albums/Stadiums/MLB/Images/Coors_Field.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Coors Field</a> <br/> <br/>:-(</td>', 'For those curious, I suspect it was the upper portion of the scoreboard, which you can see here in this daytime photo taken from a fairly similar angle: Coors Field  :-(', '2006-07-16 12:28:41.000000', NULL, 0),
