(2634281, 358881, 48228, '<td valign="top">I really like the softness of this, as it give us another perspective to it, rather than just a normal of the run fireworks image..... <br/>It almost looks like a painting, and I like that effect.....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-18 21:16:37.</i></td>', 'I really like the softness of this, as it give us another perspective to it, rather than just a normal of the run fireworks image..... It almost looks like a painting, and I like that effect.....', '2006-07-18 22:15:48.000000', '2006-07-18 22:16:37.000000', 0),
(2634900, 358714, 19670, '<td valign="top">Great shot! The horizon looks a bit tilted, though.</td>', 'Great shot! The horizon looks a bit tilted, though.', '2006-07-19 01:15:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2635143, 358922, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>WOW!  You did better than I did with my fireworks attempts.  I didn''t enter because mine all sucked, but this is nice!<br/> <br/>The clarity and sharpness of the shot is very well done and I like the colors very much.<br/> <br/>Reading the comments I would have to agree that the negative space in this shot doesn''t work that well for the shot.  You aren''t using the rule of thirds to draw my eye into a certain area, there are no real leading lines in or out of the shot and the overall composition due to either the crop or lack of crop leaves me wondering what to do with all that extra space.  A tighter crop to possibly bring the fireworks more to the center might really help this shot.  Also just a bump n the contrast or curves or levels to really make the colors pop might make more people stand up and say, "WOW!" insteadk, "Yeah, that''s nice."<br/> <br/>Hope my comments help, looking through your portfolio you have some wonderful shots, a real eye for some of this.  Welcome to DPC and Good Luck In Future Challenges.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! WOW!  You did better than I did with my fireworks attempts.  I didn''t enter because mine all sucked, but this is nice! The clarity and sharpness of the shot is very well done and I like the colors very much. Reading the comments I would have to agree that the negative space in this shot doesn''t work that well for the shot.  You aren''t using the rule of thirds to draw my eye into a certain area, there are no real leading lines in or out of the shot and the overall composition due to either the crop or lack of crop leaves me wondering what to do with all that extra space.  A tighter crop to possibly bring the fireworks more to the center might really help this shot.  Also just a bump n the contrast or curves or levels to really make the colors pop might make more people stand up and say, "WOW!" insteadk, "Yeah, that''s nice." Hope my comments help, looking through your portfolio you have some wonderful shots, a real eye for some of this.  Welcome to DPC and Good Luck In Future Challenges. Deannda', '2006-07-19 01:42:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2636045, 358795, 16046, '<td valign="top">Nice work, great finish and score.</td>', 'Nice work, great finish and score.', '2006-07-19 04:31:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2636174, 359334, 20462, '<td valign="top">no complaiints and deserved top 3 regardless of personal feelings...</td>', 'no complaiints and deserved top 3 regardless of personal feelings...', '2006-07-19 05:32:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2637725, 359314, 32321, '<td valign="top">Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First Impression:<br/>Nice clean lines, nice colours and lighting<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/>Perspective of monument seems un-natural. Right side vertical, Left side significant lean. May be optically correct from where you took the picture, but it feels uncomfortable for the viewer. Rotating the picture a few degrees CCW would make it less noticeable.<br/>Too bad you could not have captured the bust in the top third of the frame.<br/> <br/>Subject:<br/>Meets challenge<br/> <br/>Technical:<br/>Not sure what you did in terms of post processing, but based on your 10 entry, you did do some. Colours, contrast, focus and DOF are really well done.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>You may want to move the burst and add picture to your portfolio. Would be a really great shot!<br/> <br/>Summary:<br/>Congratulations on your 11th place finish and your first 6+ shot!<br/></td>', 'Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club. First Impression:Nice clean lines, nice colours and lighting Composition:Perspective of monument seems un-natural. Right side vertical, Left side significant lean. May be optically correct from where you took the picture, but it feels uncomfortable for the viewer. Rotating the picture a few degrees CCW would make it less noticeable.Too bad you could not have captured the bust in the top third of the frame. Subject:Meets challenge Technical:Not sure what you did in terms of post processing, but based on your 10 entry, you did do some. Colours, contrast, focus and DOF are really well done. Suggestions:You may want to move the burst and add picture to your portfolio. Would be a really great shot! Summary:Congratulations on your 11th place finish and your first 6+ shot!', '2006-07-19 13:02:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2637864, 358229, 55956, '<td valign="top">* Greetings from critique Club *<br/> <br/>Hi, write a critique on an image from a contest where the subject are fireworks is very difficult because the traditional evaluation criteria often are by passed.<br/>I think that is a good image, the composition is classic and there aren''t overexposure areas. The colours are tenuous and pleasant. <br/>About the frame I prefer a thinner line. the photograph is good in the complex but it lacks an element that the face to notice between the others.<br/>Best Regards<br/>Gennaro</td>', '* Greetings from critique Club * Hi, write a critique on an image from a contest where the subject are fireworks is very difficult because the traditional evaluation criteria often are by passed.I think that is a good image, the composition is classic and there aren''t overexposure areas. The colours are tenuous and pleasant. About the frame I prefer a thinner line. the photograph is good in the complex but it lacks an element that the face to notice between the others.Best RegardsGennaro', '2006-07-19 13:38:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2638796, 358474, 23203, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club<br/> <br/>A brave improvisation, but with most entries managing to capture real and fancy fireworks, this one did not catch attention. <br/> <br/>Good luck in future challenges</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club A brave improvisation, but with most entries managing to capture real and fancy fireworks, this one did not catch attention.  Good luck in future challenges', '2006-07-19 17:31:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639104, 358713, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>As I said in my original comment, it''s kinda too bad that there is so much of the building in the shot.  It kinda overpowers the whole subject of the image which to me is the fireworks.  Other than that, this is still a very nice composition.<br/> <br/>Technical notes:  It appears as I look closer that you desaturated the building.  I am wondering why you would do this?  Is it to give more attention to the fireworks themselves?  I''m not sure that this really adds to the shot and the more I look at it, the more distracted I am by it.  I notice that you shot in bulb mode.  It appears to me that you are a touch overexposed.  Your fireworks are mostly blown out.  I had the same issue with my entry.  You can tell that the fireworks are blown by the lack of color and by the dullness of the color that is left.<br/> <br/>All in all a very nice shot and a decent score for a speed challenge!<br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: As I said in my original comment, it''s kinda too bad that there is so much of the building in the shot.  It kinda overpowers the whole subject of the image which to me is the fireworks.  Other than that, this is still a very nice composition. Technical notes:  It appears as I look closer that you desaturated the building.  I am wondering why you would do this?  Is it to give more attention to the fireworks themselves?  I''m not sure that this really adds to the shot and the more I look at it, the more distracted I am by it.  I notice that you shot in bulb mode.  It appears to me that you are a touch overexposed.  Your fireworks are mostly blown out.  I had the same issue with my entry.  You can tell that the fireworks are blown by the lack of color and by the dullness of the color that is left. All in all a very nice shot and a decent score for a speed challenge!YoursTC', '2006-07-19 18:28:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639169, 359007, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Wow!  You sure this is your first time?  Not bad, not bad at all, well done!  <br/> <br/>I like the colors, very nice, a touch, just a teeeny, tiny touch of contrast might bring them out just a bit more.  The composition and crop leave me wanting though.  There is a large amount of negative space that doesn''t compliment the fireworks.  Negative space can be your friend but in this instance, to me personally, the space left of the right side of the fireworks is too much.  If you were to crop that out, using the rule of thirds, placing the firworks on the right third or even cropping off on the left, centering the firworks more, this would, to me, compliment the shot much better.  The lights on the bottom are also a bit distracting, they are there, fuzzy but don''t add anything to the shot for me.  I would have cropped them out completely.<br/> <br/>If you play with this some on the cropping, I would love to see the results.  Also, I would sharpen it just a bit, to really bring out the edges on the fireworks, not a lot, just a tiny touch.<br/> <br/>But again, for a first time effort, this is a wonderful shot.  I wish I could shoot fireworks this well, LOL :)<br/> <br/>Looking at your other work, you are going to be a force to reckon with here on DPC!  Well done!<br/> <br/>Hope my comments help and Good Luck in Future Challenges.<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Wow!  You sure this is your first time?  Not bad, not bad at all, well done!   I like the colors, very nice, a touch, just a teeeny, tiny touch of contrast might bring them out just a bit more.  The composition and crop leave me wanting though.  There is a large amount of negative space that doesn''t compliment the fireworks.  Negative space can be your friend but in this instance, to me personally, the space left of the right side of the fireworks is too much.  If you were to crop that out, using the rule of thirds, placing the firworks on the right third or even cropping off on the left, centering the firworks more, this would, to me, compliment the shot much better.  The lights on the bottom are also a bit distracting, they are there, fuzzy but don''t add anything to the shot for me.  I would have cropped them out completely. If you play with this some on the cropping, I would love to see the results.  Also, I would sharpen it just a bit, to really bring out the edges on the fireworks, not a lot, just a tiny touch. But again, for a first time effort, this is a wonderful shot.  I wish I could shoot fireworks this well, LOL :) Looking at your other work, you are going to be a force to reckon with here on DPC!  Well done! Hope my comments help and Good Luck in Future Challenges. Deannda', '2006-07-19 18:38:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639259, 358964, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>WOW!  Nice capture!  Very well done indeed, capturing the colors of our country and such a nice arrangement on top of it.  Must have been worth it to schmooze your way up, LOL! :)<br/> <br/>I really do like the colors and the moment the shot was captured, but like others, the white is a bit blown out, hard to deal with in any shot even in post processing but I can tell also that if the white wasn''t blown out  a bit the reds and blues would have been much less noticable.  Hard choices to make.  Something else I noticed was the green dots at the bottom.  A bit distracting to me, a slightly tighter crop to take them out or to clone them out would help a bit. <br/> <br/>The last thing I noticed was the balance of the shot.  You have no control over the line on the top, LOL and that''s not what bothered me.  It took a moment of looking to figure it out but then it hit me, like a shovel in the face, and btw, that really hurt ;-P<br/> <br/>Anyway, what I noticed was the negative space on the left compared to the right.  On the right the blue is coming right to the edge of the shot or very close to it.  While on the right it''s not even close.  The rule of thirds doesn''t apply here so it looks a touch off balance as a result.  The lines where the fireworks are coming up give you the level feeling so the rising left to right line of the top doesn''t botther me but the amount of space on either side is a bit bothersome.<br/> <br/>That''s all I have to say except again, WOW!  Nice overall capture, with just a few cropping adjustments and/or cloning you have a fantastically wonderful shot here that I would be proud to put up on my wall!<br/> <br/>Hope my comments help and good luck in future challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! WOW!  Nice capture!  Very well done indeed, capturing the colors of our country and such a nice arrangement on top of it.  Must have been worth it to schmooze your way up, LOL! :) I really do like the colors and the moment the shot was captured, but like others, the white is a bit blown out, hard to deal with in any shot even in post processing but I can tell also that if the white wasn''t blown out  a bit the reds and blues would have been much less noticable.  Hard choices to make.  Something else I noticed was the green dots at the bottom.  A bit distracting to me, a slightly tighter crop to take them out or to clone them out would help a bit.  The last thing I noticed was the balance of the shot.  You have no control over the line on the top, LOL and that''s not what bothered me.  It took a moment of looking to figure it out but then it hit me, like a shovel in the face, and btw, that really hurt ;-P Anyway, what I noticed was the negative space on the left compared to the right.  On the right the blue is coming right to the edge of the shot or very close to it.  While on the right it''s not even close.  The rule of thirds doesn''t apply here so it looks a touch off balance as a result.  The lines where the fireworks are coming up give you the level feeling so the rising left to right line of the top doesn''t botther me but the amount of space on either side is a bit bothersome. That''s all I have to say except again, WOW!  Nice overall capture, with just a few cropping adjustments and/or cloning you have a fantastically wonderful shot here that I would be proud to put up on my wall! Hope my comments help and good luck in future challenges! Deannda', '2006-07-19 18:51:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640477, 358822, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Not a bad shot here. Nice to havethe land in thepic to give extra dimension. The framing of the fireworks works well here and the fireworks themselves are fairly attractive. Maybe tweaking the hue and saturation to give a more vibrant color to the streams would hav ebeen nice. But a good shot overall.</td>', 'Trading Post - Not a bad shot here. Nice to havethe land in thepic to give extra dimension. The framing of the fireworks works well here and the fireworks themselves are fairly attractive. Maybe tweaking the hue and saturation to give a more vibrant color to the streams would hav ebeen nice. But a good shot overall.', '2006-07-19 23:30:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640531, 358708, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading POst - Nice shot. These are so tough to catch in full frame. You caughta nice combo of fireworks and the star is cool. Had it not been so tight and out of frame you would have scored better I believe. A tweak inthe sat onthe red channel may have helped it be a bit morevibrant as well. Good shot overall though.</td>', 'Trading POst - Nice shot. These are so tough to catch in full frame. You caughta nice combo of fireworks and the star is cool. Had it not been so tight and out of frame you would have scored better I believe. A tweak inthe sat onthe red channel may have helped it be a bit morevibrant as well. Good shot overall though.', '2006-07-19 23:45:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2647225, 358714, 48717, '<td valign="top">Just now seeing this...good job dude!</td>', 'Just now seeing this...good job dude!', '2006-07-21 20:16:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2648911, 359158, 30982, '<td valign="top">Hey - nice finish, new personal best, and a way cool photo, too!</td>', 'Hey - nice finish, new personal best, and a way cool photo, too!', '2006-07-22 14:53:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2649691, 359068, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Margie, I''m catching up on my CTP2 comments. <br/> <br/>This was a difficult challenge in which to stand out. There''s only so many views of a fireworks display to be had. Unfortunately, this entry was so different that it no longer truly met the challenge. To top it off, there is a lot of image grain to drag it further down. After seeing so many well done lightning shots in other challenges, this one just kinda sinks to the bottom. If you don''t have it already, Neat Image is worth the investment, and stick closer to the spirit of the challenge.</td>', 'Hi Margie, I''m catching up on my CTP2 comments.  This was a difficult challenge in which to stand out. There''s only so many views of a fireworks display to be had. Unfortunately, this entry was so different that it no longer truly met the challenge. To top it off, there is a lot of image grain to drag it further down. After seeing so many well done lightning shots in other challenges, this one just kinda sinks to the bottom. If you don''t have it already, Neat Image is worth the investment, and stick closer to the spirit of the challenge.', '2006-07-22 19:48:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2649716, 358714, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Shailesh! Congrats on making page one! I liked this shot because it gave the fireworks a context, a sense of place and event. If I have to nitpick, the horizon isn''t quite level and I would prefer that the top of the fireworks not be cut off. I grew up around Bloomington and I don''t recognize this location, where is it?</td>', 'Hi Shailesh! Congrats on making page one! I liked this shot because it gave the fireworks a context, a sense of place and event. If I have to nitpick, the horizon isn''t quite level and I would prefer that the top of the fireworks not be cut off. I grew up around Bloomington and I don''t recognize this location, where is it?', '2006-07-22 20:03:50.000000', NULL, 0);
